51-tools-parity: the REPL and sprite-exec against curry.eval on the goals
of one module.

Seam: sprite-exec with -g and with main, the REPL (python -m curry.tools.icy)
fed from a pipe with :load, goals, :type and :quit, then curry.eval,
curry.compile(mode='expr') for the goal with where ins free, and
curry.typeof, on the same goals.
Sources: memo A22; catalogue P46, P47, P48; the REPL page; the sprite-exec
page.
Backends: py, cxx.  Oracle: oracle.out (PAKCS 3.4.1 on coin, three,
nothing, boom and the rule goal).

Expected output: the three tools print 0 and 1 for coin, nothing for
nothing, and 3 for three and main; the REPL and the API print the rule
goal as {ins=["x"]} "cmd1" and {ins=["y", "z"]} "cmd2" and the type as
coin :: Int.  For boom, sprite-exec prints "** boom **" on stderr and
exits 1 (the run script prints the status), the REPL prints its error
report on stderr (not compared), and the API raises EvaluationError with
the message boom (P46: one error, three reports).  Pins no defect.
